Description: Fix incomplete mitigation for React Server Components DoS (GHSA-5j59-xgg2-r9c4)
 The prior fix for CVE-2025-55184 was incomplete: a crafted Server Function
 payload could still drive the RSC deserializer into an unbounded loop when
 inspecting chunked thenables, causing sustained CPU consumption (CWE-400).
 This backports the cycle-protection counter (facebook/react#35351, next.js
 upstream 7c1be85) into the vendored react-server-dom-{webpack,turbopack}
 server bundles. Because target 14.2.2's Chunk.prototype.then lacks the
 recursive-thenable inspection loop entirely, the full guarded inspection
 loop (with the > 1000 iteration cap) is hand-ported into the INITIALIZED
 resolution path across all server build variants.
